# Cloudflare Pages' response headers, as Hedge School's and Cyanotype's (their static/_headers). Pages reads this file
# and does not serve it.

# Search engines index the live address only (docs/design/23-search.md). Cloudflare's own addresses for the project
# (its pages.dev address) and for each preview (dev.<its pages.dev address>, a commit's hash) answer with noindex, so
# that no copy of a page competes with the live one. Each page also names its live address as canonical. Until the
# site's launch, these are its only addresses (docs/design/34-tak-site.md, "How the site stays unlaunched").
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Files whose paths change when their content does: the build's hashed code. Browsers keep them for a year without
# asking again.
/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
